Z||000000||gt boy||08-19-2001||01:38 PM||||so....a buddy of mine just had to drive my car to see what it was like. <P>when he came back it smelt terrible and the wheels where hot..to my suprise he had left the e-brake on...stupid a$$. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>now the brakes feel spongy...so what has my former friend done to my brakes?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-19-2001||02:39 PM||||He over-heated them. Try bleeding the brakes.<BR>It most likely has air in the lines. When brakes over-heat the small air bubbles expand<BR>and the brakes get mushy/soft.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jncomutt||08-19-2001||02:41 PM||||Anytime I take the car anywhere, for anything, inwhich someone else has to drive, they always leave the damn thing on.. Even If if I tell them to make sure it down.  (I guess they don't understand the having to pull it up to put it down thing)  Places such as getting my windshield changed, emmissions, servicing, etc.  What I found one time is that I was told the brake fluid got too hot and ?boiled?  I'm not sure if this actually happened, but I had the crazy brake feel afterwards too... I just rebled em, they were fine..||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||03:05 PM||||may have to sand glaze off pads, worse thing maybe warped the rotors.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gt boy||08-19-2001||03:36 PM||||i will try bleeding them ..that sounds like the easiest way first.<P>thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||08-19-2001||06:10 PM||||Probally didn't get hot enough, but better now than later having to rebuild calipers...<P>Check your slider pins, the calipers should move when you push them by hand (with the front unbolted of course...)<P>Good time to completely flush the system and put in new dot 4 fluid.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
